00:49:12.093 --> 00:49:13.210
I was right about the thesis.

00:49:13.210 --> 00:49:14.710
I was wrong about the executive.

00:49:14.710 --> 00:49:17.330
I needed to learn that,

00:49:17.330 --> 00:49:19.680
I would always put myself
in the jockey position,

00:49:19.680 --> 00:49:21.510
I would know how to operate it.

00:49:21.510 --> 00:49:22.700
So I needed to learn that.

00:49:22.700 --> 00:49:24.200
That's where I made a lot of my mistakes.

00:49:24.200 --> 00:49:26.540
The concept was right,
the operator was wrong.

00:49:26.540 --> 00:49:28.266
Especially at that early of a stage,

00:49:28.266 --> 00:49:30.350
when you go later it's a bit easier.

00:49:30.350 --> 00:49:32.885
Did you have a common mistake
early on in your career?

00:49:32.885 --> 00:49:36.615
- There's always a learning
curve when you're younger.

00:49:36.615 --> 00:49:37.720
- [Gary] Yes always.

00:49:37.720 --> 00:49:40.320
- When you're in your 20's,
you're in a lot of risk.

00:49:41.407 --> 00:49:42.450
Because you don't know enough yet.

00:49:42.450 --> 00:49:44.862
You're just as smart
as you'll ever will be.

00:49:44.862 --> 00:49:49.316
But you don't have the context
to make those decisions.

00:49:49.316 --> 00:49:50.330
- I apologize,

00:49:50.330 --> 00:49:54.440
do you then believe that
that's a very good decade

00:49:54.440 --> 00:49:57.120
to actually be in a
high risk, high reward,

00:49:57.120 --> 00:49:59.364
