00:50:07.450 --> 00:50:10.130
Do you think that kids
at 22 to 30 are being

00:50:10.130 --> 00:50:13.020
too conservative over
the last several decades

00:50:13.020 --> 00:50:15.945
because they're supposed
to be in the real world,

00:50:15.945 --> 00:50:18.080
versus actually taking
advantage of that decade

00:50:18.080 --> 00:50:21.164
with the over lay of gathering context.

00:50:21.164 --> 00:50:26.160
- It's high risk strategy
to take the approach

00:50:26.160 --> 00:50:28.510
that you're talking about because if you

00:50:28.510 --> 00:50:31.000
just stumble from mistake to mistake

00:50:32.949 --> 00:50:34.330
and you're not particularly

00:50:34.330 --> 00:50:36.948
gifted like yourself, where
you can't self correct,

00:50:36.948 --> 00:50:41.238
that you end up with no
fundamental skills of any type.

00:50:41.238 --> 00:50:45.320
And then you're like a
lost soul in your 30's.

00:50:47.000 --> 00:50:49.530
- But you would agree
with me that many struggle

00:50:49.530 --> 00:50:51.425
with the relationship with time

00:50:51.425 --> 00:50:52.520
that being in your in your 30's is still

00:50:52.520 --> 00:50:53.810
uncomfortably young.

00:50:53.810 --> 00:50:58.810
- Yes but I was never
smarter than I was 32.

00:50:59.090 --> 00:51:00.160
That's your max--

00:51:00.160 --> 00:51:01.654
- Is that your number?

00:51:01.654 --> 00:51:02.670
- Yes.

00:51:02.670 --> 00:51:03.927
- Shit.

00:51:03.927 --> 00:51:06.190
- That's when you think
you are the smartest person

00:51:06.190 --> 00:51:07.332
in the world, when you're 32.

00:51:07.332 --> 00:51:08.507
- [Gary] 'Cause fuck at 34 I think I am.

00:51:08.507 --> 00:51:09.340
(laughter)

00:51:09.340 --> 00:51:11.710
- Now the fact is, you're not.

00:51:11.710 --> 00:51:13.978
But you've accumulated enough knowledge

00:51:13.978 --> 00:51:17.061
